"List/Edit" V7.2 for Psion S3 & S3A by Andy Grieve
--------------------------------------------------

For XP or LZ model organisers, look for LISTED.ZIP on Compuserve, or
Imperial College.  (See Sources below).

Installation
------------
        Copy LISTED.OPA into the \APP directory for the S3A version.
        Copy LISTEDS3.OPA into the \APP directory for the S3 version.

        Make directory \LST
        Copy SAMPLE.LST into the \LST directory.

        Install Application from the System Apps menu (see Psion Manual).

        Look at the SAMPLE list, Help, and the Menu.

        Create new lists using 'New File' option from main menu.

        'Assign Button' to allow easy switching to your lists (Ctrl-Data?).

        The program LISTCONV is provided to allow you to convert old LISTS
        from previous versions of LISTED (before V7.0) into the new format
        and directory. If you didn't use the old version of LISTED, you
        won't need LISTCONV.

Keys
----
        [Help] gives help on quick keys.
        [Home] and [End] go to the top or bottom of a list.
        Cursor left and right go one screen up or down a list.
        Cursor up and down move up and down one record.
                Current record is at the top of the screen after '->'.
        [Enter] edits the current record.
        [Delete] deletes the current record.
        [Tab] allows you to go directly to a particular record.
        [Space] allows you to find a particular record on S3a, or add a
                record on S3.  [Space] again finds next.
        [Menu] shows a menu of options (with other short keys).
        {Diamond} key (next to menu key on S3a) allows you to add a new
                record.

Updates
-------
        Now handles more fields per record.
        Added a Menu with 'quick keys'.
        Automatically adds ' . . .' to records with extra fields.
        Changed default directory to \LST from \ODB
        Changed default file extension to .LST from .ODB
        Changed Edit dialog for clarity about 'extra' fields.
        Records can be 'Copied' to temporary storeage, then Inserted again,
                even to different file if you switch using [Psion-N.]
        Deleted records can now be 'Inserted' back into file with [Psion-I].
        'Purge File (del)' is now 'Kill File (del)'.
        Psion-H shows Help panel.
        'Hidden' Records can be stored without an entry in the first field.

